ction during normal business hours, and posted on the website of the Commissioner. Each summary shall also be available to the public, on request, by fax or mail. 24. (1) The summary shall : (a)subject to subsection (3), set out the source and nature, but not the value, of the income, assets and liabilities referred to in the Member’s statement filed under section 20;(b) identify any contracts or subcontracts referred to in paragraph 21(1)(c) and describe their subject-matter and nature;(c) list the names of any affiliated corporations referred to in that statement; (d) include a copy of any statements of disclosure filed by the Member under subsections 14(3), 15(1) and 21(3); (e) list the positions and corporations, trade or professional associations and trade unions disclosed under paragraph 21(1)(e); and (f) list any trusts disclosed under paragraph 21(1)(b.1). Andréanne Larouche · Member of Parliament OCIEC Translation Declaration type Disclosure Summaries (Code) Disclosure date May 20, 2026 Regime Conflict of Interest Code for Members of the House of Commons Description LiabilitiesCar loan with DesjardinsSpouse's/Common-Law Partner's assetsSole ownership of a residential rental unit located in Sutton, QuebecShares of:- ADOBE INC- ALIMENTATION COUCHE-TARD - ALPHABET INC CL-A- APPLE INC - BERKSHIRE HATHAWAY-B-NEW- LVMH MOET HENNESSY LO-ADR- MASTERCARD INC CL-A - METRO INC - MICROSOFT CORP - BANQUE NATIONALE DU CDA- NIKE INC CL-B - PEPSICO INC - ROGERS COMMUNICATION-B NV Spouse's/Common-Law Partner's liabilitiesMortgage with DesjardinsSpouse's/Common-Law Partner's activitiesDirector of the Musée des communications et d’histoire de Sutton Disclosed on May 20, 2026","url":"https://www.ethicscanada.ca/en/public-registry/Details?declarationId=c6f0c89b-e147-f111-81a8-001dd8b72449"}],"other":[]},"lobbying":{"total":258,"first":"2020-01-30","last":"2026-10-20","byYear":{"2020":17,"2021":9,"2022":19,"2023":29,"2024":69,"2025":53,"2026":62},"topSubjects":[["Health",35],["A